Z||000005||kyote||12-24-2001||07:18 AM||||Like terryk said.. Code 12 means all data from sensors was normal.. <BR>But just because it does not have a code stored means that nothing is wrong..<BR>IF.. something is wrong, it is with a component that does not get monitored with a sensor..<BR>You are gonna have to enlighten us  on what is happening when you say "your baby" is hurting .....<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="blue">'84 SE</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">'84 SE (Strictly Parts Car)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">'86 SE</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">'00 HD 1200XL Sportster</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||12-24-2001||12:11 PM||||You will always get the code 12.  It will always start with that, then display any other codes.  If all you get is a 12, then no error codes are stored in your ECM.||||reg||1
